* Sun Oct 04 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.5.3-1
- The entry page shows edited values at once
- Saving an entry or group waits for a running sync merge

* Sun Oct 04 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.5.2-1
- Security: a merged database with other credentials can no longer set the
  sync server; sync settings run only once confirmed on this phone

* Sun Oct 04 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.5.1-1
- Shorter pulley menu; sync, merging, the Bitwarden import and About moved
  to a Settings page

* Sun Oct 04 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.5.0-1
- Sync with your own Nextcloud: log in through the browser or with an app
  password, missing folders are created, changes from both sides are
  merged, offline changes sync when the connection is back
- Self-signed server certificates only after confirming their fingerprint
- Merge a copy of the database from a file, with its own password and key
  file if needed
- New permission: Internet, used only for Nextcloud sync

* Sun Oct 04 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.4.0-1
- Add KDBX 3.1 databases: they are stored as KDBX 4 with Argon2id at a
  chosen protection level; the original file stays unchanged

* Sun Oct 04 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.3.0-1
- Create new databases with Argon2id at three protection levels
- Keep databases and key files in the app's private storage; add existing
  files by unlocking them once, save copies to Documents or Downloads,
  delete stored databases
- About page with version, license and third-party notices
- Security and robustness fixes from a review before the Harbour submission
- Faster list loading and import merging
- Explain how to convert KDBX 3.1 databases in KeePassXC

* Sat Oct 03 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.2.0-1
- Create, edit, move and delete entries; history and recycle bin as in KeePassXC
- Create, rename and move groups
- Restore entries and groups from the recycle bin, and empty it
- View earlier versions of an entry
- Atomic, verified saves with the last three versions kept as backups
- Password generator
- Import Bitwarden and Vaultwarden JSON exports, unencrypted or password-protected;
  a repeated import merges into the earlier one

* Sat Oct 03 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.1.0-1
- First version: open KDBX 4 databases read-only with password and key file
